{
	"$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
	// Its own tiny Worker, deliberately separate from freeroll-app — see index.js for why.
	"name": "freeroll-bot-tick",
	"compatibility_date": "2026-08-24",
	"main": "index.js"
	// Cron Trigger temporarily removed here — Cloudflare's own dashboard/API confirmed the
	// */5 * * * * schedule was registered correctly (GET .../schedules showed it, deploy logs
	// confirmed it) but never actually fired once in 8+ hours: GraphQL invocation analytics for
	// freeroll-bot-tick showed zero cron-sourced invocations the whole time. That's a stuck
	// registration on Cloudflare's side, not a config problem. Clearing it via a deploy with no
	// `triggers` key (this commit), then restoring it in a following commit, forces a real
	// delete+recreate cycle instead of the no-op re-PUT a second `wrangler deploy` of the same
	// config would do. See bot-traffic-simulation memory / PR #25 for the full history.
}
